  "maps": {
    "mixamo": {
      "label": "Mixamo",
      "reference": "skeletons/mixamo.json",
      "units": "cm",
      "bindPose": "T",
      "verified": false,

      "notes": [
        "NAMES ARE THE LOADED ONES, NOT THE AUTHORED ONES. Mixamo names its bones 'mixamorig:Hips'; three's FBXLoader strips the colon and you get 'mixamorigHips'. Writing the map against what you see in Blender produces a map that matches nothing.",
        "NEVER LOOK BONES UP BY NAME IN A MIXAMO FBX. The loader emits a same-named leaf child for every bone — 117 nodes for a 52-bone skeleton — so getObjectByName is ambiguous. Work from skeleton.bones, which holds 52 unique names.",
        "The mesh is split by material (Alpha_Surface, Alpha_Joints) and three builds a SEPARATE Skeleton for each. They share a rest pose; take either.",
        "MIXAMO HAS NO ROOT BONE. Its Hips carries the translation that our 'root' carries, which is why 'root' has no entry here and why root motion needs handling as its own step rather than falling out of the map.",
        "T-pose, same as ours, and the limb axes match — upper arm [1,0,0], thigh [0,-1,0] on both. The rest-pose delta is therefore near identity for the body, which is the expensive half of a retarget arriving nearly free.",
        "Handedness matches: Mixamo Left is our _l, no mirroring. Checked by X sign, because getting this wrong is silent and survives a long way."
      ],

      "proportions": {
        "hips": { "source": 99.8, "ours": 0.917, "note": "cm vs m — the ratio after unit conversion is ~0.92, so hip translation needs scaling, not just rotating." },
        "ankle": { "source": 10.5, "ours": 0.104, "note": "Ankles match almost exactly. Leg length is close enough that foot contact should not drift badly." }
      },

      "bones": {
        "mixamorigHips": "pelvis",

