    "ue5": {
      "label": "Unreal Engine 5",
      "reference": "skeletons/ue5-mannequin.json",
      "units": "cm",
      "bindPose": "A",
      "verified": false,

      "notes": [
        "THE NAMES ARE OURS ALREADY, THE BONES ARE NOT. Our skeleton borrowed Unreal's names, but our bind is a T-pose and the mannequin's an A-pose, and Unreal has five spine bones and two neck bones to our three and one. So this is a real retarget through the rest pose, not a rename.",
        "OURS 3 SPINE ONTO THEIR 5: spine_01, spine_03, spine_05. spine_02 and spine_04 are left at rest and ride the bone below them; neck_02 the same under neck_01. Their head is lower-case.",
        "THE ROOT TRAVELS. Theirs splits travel from bob as ours does, root on the floor and pelvis under it, so root goes to root (root motion works) and the pelvis lands under it where ours is.",
        "LEFT AT REST: the metacarpals (the fingers are mapped from their first joint), the twist bones (Unreal's post-process graph drives them), the ik_ bones, interaction and center_of_mass.",
        "THE REFERENCE IS DATA, NOT EPIC'S FILE. Names, parents and rest read off SKM_Manny_Simple.FBX by scripts/extract-skeleton.mjs; Manny and Quinn share the skeleton."
      ],

      "bones": {
